&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forward Deployed AI Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global AI Strategy &amp;amp; Solutions defines how DEPT®’s clients respond as AI agents become the primary layer between customers and brands. The Future of the Customer Journey (FCJ) is the team’s flagship offer: it maps how AI systems intermediate customer journeys, diagnoses where a brand’s product reality diverges from what AI systems say about it, and directs investment accordingly. Growth and strategy teams across markets are selling and delivering it now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;Forward Deployed AI Engineer, you are an embedded builder inside that motion. You will sit with growth and strategy teams, understand the problem in front of them, and answer with working software rather than documentation. You will convert FCJ methodology into agentic components, prototypes, and internal tools, and integrate with infrastructure that lets new prototypes appear in days. When needed, you will work across global client projects on a partially billable basis, making sure the firm-wide strategy is captured and implemented properly rather than reinvented market by market. As components mature, you will collaborate with product and craft teams to keep everything compatible with the long-term platform and hand over cleanly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be given broad problem statements to help collaborate and solve, not specific product ideas and features to create. We are not looking for someone to lead on devops or CI/CD, this is about having great ideas that are sensitive to our clients’ real challenges, and shipping prototypes and strategic tools rapidly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your most important collaboration is with the FCJ core team on the global growth strategy: deciding what gets built next, for which market, to unlock which engagement. The toolchain will keep changing underneath you, new models, new vendor products, new technology-partner platforms, and that is the point. This role suits an engineer who learns by shipping and treats every new AI product as something to master in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the FCJ core team on the global growth strategy, converting methodology into working agentic components, prototypes, and internal tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with growth and strategy teams to understand their problems and provide working solutions at prototype pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across global client projects on a partially billable basis, ensuring the firm-wide FCJ strategy is captured and implemented consistently across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product and craft teams where necessary to document integration paths, maintain platform compatibility, and hand over validated components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technology partners to evaluate, adopt, and integrate new AI products; maintain an AI-native toolchain and share what works across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience prototyping and shipping software in any modern backend language (Python, TypeScript, Go, or similar), with the ability to leverage AI tooling to spin up prototype frontends and APIs quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building applications across the mainstream LLM model families (Gemini, GPT, Claude), connecting models to enterprise data and tools using patterns such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and skills-based agent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in working with APIs to connect different services, authentication, data exchange, and integration across platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing agentic systems with orchestration frameworks such as LangChain, LangGraph, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native way of working: AI tooling is the default across coding, research, and delivery, with comfort spanning the tools in use across different markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a forward-deployed, customer engineering, solutions engineering, or applied AI role within an agency, consultancy, or AI company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting working software to non-technical stakeholders, including strategists and clients, and iterating live on their feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of emerging integration standards such as OpenAPI and Model Context Protocol (MCP) for connecting agents to business systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of any of the following: paid media, social platforms, user behaviour, agentic commerce, or generative engine optimisation (GEO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with evaluation, tracing, and observability for LLM applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated learning mindset: a record of adopting new AI products from technology partners quickly, learning by doing rather than waiting for training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible, hybrid working policy (2 days from the office in London).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent salary based on experience and equal pay policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension, free private healthcare, mental health support, and company sick pay scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days paid holiday (plus UK Bank Holidays).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help getting you to work with a season ticket loan and cycle to work scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced family friendly policies to support new parents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social and Cultural Events, plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues through organised activities and celebrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspirational Talks, bringing the outside in with regular guest speakers and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development, supporting your growth with continuous opportunities to learn and advance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buddy Programme: You will be paired with a ‘Buddy’ to help you through your first weeks’ at DEPT®.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/en-gb/insight/dept-is-a-certified-b-corporation/&quot;&gt;B Corp® since 2021&lt;/a&gt; and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global annual &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/dept-cares-day-2023/&quot;&gt;DEPT® Cares Month&lt;/a&gt; in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why DEPT®?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Enterprise Solutions designs, builds, and operates the growth systems that competitive businesses rely on. In a world where Al is reshaping how companies drive growth, we lead clients in business transformation and marketing modernization, connecting strategy directly to execution. Our 12,000 experts in engineering and platforms, commerce, consulting, content transformation, CRM, and CX work within a unified global operating unit across 40+ markets. WPP Enterprise Solutions works alongside best-in-class partners including Adobe, AWS, Braze, Google, Microsoft, Salesforce, and Shopify, as well as innovators in AI, to deliver growth solutions tailored to the needs of our clients’ businesses. VML, part of WPP, supports WPP Enterprise Solutions by helping brands activate transformation through creativity and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Working in technology &amp;amp; innovation with WPP Enterprise Solutions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At WPP Enterprise Solutions Netherlands, we create connected brands to drive growth. Our expertise spans the full customer journey, with deep capabilities in commerce, consultancy, CRM, CX, data, production, technology, content, media and more. We deliver end-to-end solutions for ambitious B2B and B2C brands, supported by the wider WPP network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work combines strategy, product thinking, experience design, data, engineering and AI to solve real business problems, from enterprise commerce modernisation and digital shelf excellence to AI-enabled content operations, marketing automation, GEO, workflow orchestration and custom AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join the Product Management &amp;amp; AI Solutions team: the group that bridges business strategy, customer experience and technology to deliver scalable commerce and enterprise solutions. We work closely with UX/CX, Data &amp;amp; AI, SEO/GEO, Content, CRM, Paid and Retail Media, Engineering and Delivery teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambition is to move beyond isolated skills and build repeatable, outcome-led propositions around commerce growth topics such as Search &amp;amp; Discovery, Personalisation, CRO &amp;amp; Experience Optimisation, Product Data/PIM &amp;amp; Digital Shelf, Content Supply Chain &amp;amp; AI Content Operations, CRM &amp;amp; Lifecycle Growth, Performance &amp;amp; Retail Media, SEO/GEO and Composable Commerce Modernisation. Alongside this, we are growing our applied AI work: shaping and delivering custom AI agents and AI-enabled workflows for clients, from discovery and pilot through to production and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why this role exists&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clients are increasingly asking for integrated solutions rather than isolated delivery capacity. They need people who can understand the business problem, shape the product direction, define the right solution, translate it into clear specifications and guide teams through delivery. At the same time, AI is changing how commerce, content, marketing and operations work, creating a need for analysts who can combine structured requirements thinking with product ownership, enterprise technology understanding and the design of AI-enabled workflows and agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is designed for someone who can operate as a strong Business Analyst, step into Product Owner responsibilities when needed, advocate for product thinking inside the organisation and help turn our AI and commerce capabilities into scalable client value. You will work across both our commerce and enterprise product work and our applied AI work. The mix depends on client demand, and we expect the AI share to grow over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Business Analyst, Enterprise &amp;amp; AI Solutions, you bridge business needs, product direction and technical delivery across enterprise digital commerce and martech ecosystems. You analyse business processes, clarify user and stakeholder needs, define requirements and support solutioning across the commerce stack: CMS, Search, PIM/PXM, DAM, ERP, OMS, CDP, CRM, analytics, marketing automation, paid/media platforms and integration layers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also work on AI initiatives such as custom AI agents (for example for pricing, search or customer service), content and marketing automation, product/content enrichment, GEO and organic discoverability, AI orchestration and workflow automation. You do not need to be a machine learning engineer or a domain expert, but you must be technically curious and comfortable working with APIs, data flows, automation tools, LLM-based workflows, AI quality evaluation, governance requirements and human-in-the-loop processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your experience and the project context, you may act as a hands-on BA, a product-minded discovery partner, a proxy Product Owner or a work stream lead. In all cases, your job is to make ambiguity manageable, decisions explicit and delivery focused on measurable value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Solution Architects and Product Owners and translate business goals into clear requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, process flows, tech architecture, data flows and integration specifications that delivery teams can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across commerce, martech and enterprise ecosystems, including CMS, Search, PIM/PXM, DAM, ERP, OMS, CDP, CRM, analytics, marketing automation and media platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, shape and specify practical AI, automation and workflow orchestration opportunities across content, marketing, commerce and operational processes, from process mapping and readiness checks to a scoped pilot with a clear business case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specify AI agents and LLM-based workflows: define the task, data sources, tools and integrations, guardrails, human-in-the-loop steps and escalation paths, plus the evaluation criteria that decide when a solution is ready to go live. After launch, help measure quality, adoption and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a Business Analyst or proxy Product Owner when needed by supporting prioritisation, backlog refinement, sprint planning, UAT, release preparation and stakeholder alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect business, UX, data, SEO/GEO, content, engineering, legal and delivery teams to make sure solutions are valuable, feasible, scalable and well governed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help make our AI work repeatable and sellable: contribute to proposals, scoping and estimates, and build reusable assets such as discovery templates, requirement patterns, evaluation sets and playbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At the senior end of the role, independently lead workstreams, own parts of the client relationship and coach junior analysts or product team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured problem-solver who starts with the business problem, not only the requested feature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-minded Business Analyst who can move between discovery, specification, prioritisation and delivery support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable acting as a proxy Product Owner when a project needs stronger product ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically fluent enough to discuss APIs, data flows, integrations, platform dependencies and implementation trade-offs with engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and pragmatic about AI: you use AI tools in your own work and understand the opportunity, but also the need for governance, quality, reliability and human oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with fast-moving technology: you focus on the problem and the outcome rather than a specific tool, and you pick up new platforms quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong in workshops, stakeholder alignment and decision-making, with the confidence to challenge constructively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to represent the Product Management &amp;amp; AI Solutions team inside WPP and help other teams understand the value of product thinking and applied AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially aware: you can connect requirements and solutions to client value, efficiency, scalability, conversion, discoverability or operational impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and low-ego, with the ability to work across Commerce, UX/CX, Data, SEO/GEO, Content, CRM, Media, Engineering and Delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The basics&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience as a Business Analyst, Product Owner, Solution Analyst or similar role, ideally in commerce, martech, enterprise platforms, consulting or a digital agency environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital commerce ecosystems, preferably B2B and/or B2C enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of platforms and domains such as CMS, Search, PIM/PXM, DAM, ERP, OMS, CDP, CRM, analytics, marketing automation and paid/media technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience writing user stories, acceptance criteria, functional specifications, process flows and integration requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good technical understanding of REST APIs, web platforms, data flows, system integrations and common delivery dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on familiarity with generative AI tools and a working understanding of how LLM-based solutions behave, including their limitations and how to test the quality of their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Agile delivery environments with tools such as Jira, Confluence or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, facilitation, documentation and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent professional English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently residing in the Netherlands with a valid work permit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus points&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with automation tools such as n8n, Zapier or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping AI, LLM, agentic or workflow orchestration use cases in a business or delivery context, ideally including at least one that went live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI and agent platforms such as Microsoft Copilot Studio, Azure AI Foundry, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI or the OpenAI and Anthropic APIs, and with concepts such as retrieval (RAG), tool use and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI governance and regulation, such as the EU AI Act, and with responsible AI practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with search and personalisation platforms, composable commerce, PIM/PXM, CDP, CRM or marketing automation platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GA4, BigQuery, SQL, Python, Postman, Figma, Miro or similar tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Dutch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;In return, this is what we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get access to an international network of clients, colleagues, technology partners and resources. We have a listening ear for ambitious ideas, and together we keep stretching our boundaries. We want you to follow the path you’re building, and we invest in your personal development in a dynamic, collaborative workplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A monthly salary between &lt;strong&gt;€4,800 and €5200&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;gross, depending on your experience, seniority and fit with the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A gross annual 8% holiday allowance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to our commuting package to suit your individual needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pension benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A choice of a Mac or Windows laptop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A culture of trust, with a feel-at-home vibe and an international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health support, including complimentary membership EAP counselling services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefits (when available) including yoga classes, an in-house masseuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to work with a renowned international customer base of B2B and B2C brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence and world-class partnerships – all united by our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://wpp.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;normaltextrun&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;WPP (VML/WPP Enterprise Solutions) is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;scxw176048299&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click &quot;Submit Application&quot;, this will send any information you add below to WPP (VML/WPP Enterprise Solutions). Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;. California residents should read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build AI for engineers designing cars, medical devices, and jet engines. Products this complex aren&#39;t sketched and sent to production. Teams spend months on iterations, reviews, and tests, predicting how every part performs before anything is built. CoLab is where those reviews happen, and we capture the rationale behind every change. Other tools show what changed between versions. Only CoLab knows why. That&#39;s how our AI helps manufacturers like Bobcat, Triumph Motorcycles, and GE Appliances make better decisions, eliminate rework cycles, and get to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proudly based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab started with one customer in 2018. Since then we’ve raised a&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/ai-is-changing-engineering-colab-just-raised-72m-to-lead-the-transformation&quot;&gt; $72M Series C&lt;/a&gt;, been named the 57th fastest growing company in North America by Deloitte (&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/colab-ranked-number-57-fastest-growing-company-in-north-america-on-the-2025-deloitte-technology-fast-500&quot;&gt;Fast 500™&lt;/a&gt;), signed multi-year&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-bombardier-signs-contract-colab-ai-software/&quot;&gt; AI partnerships with companies like Bombardier&lt;/a&gt;, and grown to a team of 250+.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role that helps define how CoLab delivers technical value to its most strategic customers in Aerospace and Defence. CoLab is a category-creating product, which means adoption isn&#39;t just a rollout. It&#39;s a change in how the organization works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;d act as a trusted advisor, leveraging people, process, and technology to help teams rethink how they manage feedback, data, and decision-making across design and PLM. That means getting deep into customer workflows, testing new ways of working, and building repeatable methods the rest of the team can scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside a Customer Success Manager, and use what you learn on the front line to help shape product direction. This role isn&#39;t about selling or pitching. It&#39;s about deeply understanding engineering problems and solving them alongside the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a candidate in Switzerland to work regularly on-site with local CoLab customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a mechanical engineer by trade and have worked as a designer in an A&amp;amp;D company. You also understand the full product development life cycle: how design, manufacturing, quality, and engineering leadership depend on each other, and where collaboration breaks down. You can coach those teams toward working together better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know how to improve that life cycle with technology. Maybe you’ve championed internal tools or created automation or scripts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also know a process that makes sense on paper won’t get adopted on its own. You can meet people where they are, including the stakeholders who don’t want to change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to be the loudest voice in the room, but you can run a sprint and lead a cross-functional project. If the average person might find this job too undefined or complex, that probably excites you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mapping a customer&#39;s current-state design review and engineering workflows, and defining the target-state process their teams will actually adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying and tuning CoLab&#39;s AI capabilities against a customer&#39;s own standards, drawing checklists, and design guidelines, and diagnosing what&#39;s working and what isn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing mechanical engineering expertise to validate AI-generated results and ensure engineering rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating and solving complex engineering data and integration challenges across PLM, ERP, QMS, and traditional design feedback tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding adoption into new teams, programs, and sites within the account, partnering with the Customer Success Manager on where the next opportunity sits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with product teams to identify feature gaps, improve capabilities, and refine AutoReview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in mechanical design engineering, ideally in a medium- to large-sized organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PLM &amp;amp; ERP systems and enterprise engineering data architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical projects and cross-functional collaborations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers or internal stakeholders to solve technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in fast-changing, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and documentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of high-level AI architecture, specifically LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, data integrations, and enterprise architecture concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in Switzerland&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal tool development, scripting, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI/ML tools applied to engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in design consulting or product development at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a fully remote role, travel is a consistent part of the job. There are two primary types of travel you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Weeks:&lt;/strong&gt; Once per quarter, the sales team or entire company gets together in person. These typically involve traveling out on a Monday and returning on a Thursday or Friday. Two of these each year are held at our headquarters in St. John&#39;s, Newfoundland, Canada and the others take place in more central locations that evolve as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-sites:&lt;/strong&gt; This role will work closely with a local customer with expectations to be on site with that customer, so there will likely be far less travel than our typical MFDE roll. That being said, in the event the local customer were to no longer work with us, the following is our standard MFDE travel expectations: “For most of our large deployment customers, we will visit on-site during kick-off and key expansion opportunities. Most on-sites involve 2-3 days with the customer, with travel on either side. Travel is primarily within North America, and you can expect 4 customer on-sites per quarter.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
